1. we call the rendering kernel that will do the work for a single pixel (x,y)

2. it calls the octree traverse function which will return the block position that the ray hit, the float position where exactly the hit was and the blockId:

[x, y, z, x_f, y_f, z_f, blockId]

3. it then takes this info and gets the light color etc from blocks_data.cuh

4. renders it